     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg per day**. For adults:\n- The most ibuprofen usually given in one dose is **800 mg**.\n- The most usually given in a day is **3,200 mg** (that's 800 mg four times daily).\n\nSo each dose would be twice the usual maximum, and the daily total would be twice the usual daily limit. That carries real risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and other toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total). This is a common mix-up, where the daily total gets written as the dose.\n2. **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n3. **Something else**, such as a different dose or frequency.\n\nLet me know which one and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1600 mg four times daily on purpose, please confirm and tell me the reason, and I'll add it to the order as a note so pharmacy can review it."
      }
     ],
